# moor_expr.grammar -- Moor's expressions, one nonterminal per level
E    -> E || A | A
A    -> A && Q | Q
Q    -> Q == C | Q != C | C
C    -> C < S | C <= S | C > S | C >= S | S
S    -> S + M | S - M | M
M    -> M * U | M / U | M % U | U
U    -> - U | ! U | P
P    -> num | true | false | name | ( E )
| name ( ) | name ( Args ) | name [ E ]
Args -> E | Args , E
